Surface Apple's GrandSlam `em` message alongside the `ec` code.

apple-auth normally throws only "Apple authentication rejected (code <ec>)".
For the supervised sign-in diagnosis we also need Apple's own human-readable
message. This appends it as ` em=[<message>]` so the caller can extract and
sanitize it; the raw message never leaves the device un-sanitized. Scope is one
throw in status(); no cryptography, request construction or behaviour changes.

--- a/src/client/authentication.cpp
+++ b/src/client/authentication.cpp
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@ void status(const Json& response) {
     require(s.is_object(), "Malformed GrandSlam status");
     auto code = s.value("ec", std::int64_t(0));
     if (code != 0) {
-        throw Error("Apple authentication rejected (code " + std::to_string(code) + ")");
+        auto message = s.value("em", std::string());
+        throw Error("Apple authentication rejected (code " + std::to_string(code) +
+                    (message.empty() ? "" : (" em=[" + message + "]")) + ")");
     }
 }
 
